    {
      "id": 29409,
      "name": "EvanDan55",
      "username": "EvanDan55",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-05-02T20:53:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;awp832&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"awp832\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I dunno,  when I thought about it my mind went into the direction that RC was in trouble, so a young and budding new genius girl went to ask the old master for help.   Then he gave her the “I shall never fight again, violence is not the answer, young child”  routine and refused to help.  So Wraith (after a suitably epic fight with Spite that nearly cost her her life) would go find others willing to take action, thereby meeting up with the rest of the F5.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In Wraith’s bio it said she was contacted by the Freedom Five first; she didn’t seek them out. And I still can’t see them being on edge with each other. Even if Mr. Fixer had turned her down, why would she hold a grudge? She could literally afford the best martial arts trainers in the world. I can’t see her and him being angry with each other.</p>\n<p>However, now that I glanced back at Wraith’s bio, it says she graduated with a degree in mechanical engineering, so I’m guessing she’d get along pretty well with Unity. They’ve got some common ground.</p>",
